  "line": "I step into the lair and bow low to the dragon. Vaelrith, tell us what the knights took, and where they keep it now.",
  "ok": true,
  "problems": [],
  "replied": true,
  "replies": [
    {
      "messageId": 4,
      "speaker": "Vaelrith",
      "text": "*\"You bow. Good. Respect is a currency I still value,\"* Vaelrith rumbles, the sound vibrating through the stone floor. The dragon shifts, and for a moment the torchlight catches the dull grey of its scales—once bright enough to blind, now faded like river-stone.\n*\"They took everything. Every piece of gold, every crown, every jewel I amassed over nine centuries. But there are things in there more precious than coin.\"* The dragon's good eye narrows. *\"A harp that plays only for the grieving. The sealed egg of a rival wyrm. Letters I never sent.\"* It pauses, a flicker of something—regret, perhaps—crossing its ancient features. *\"They took the proof that my long life meant something.\"*\nA breath of thin smoke escapes Vaelrith's nostrils. *\"The Order of the Silver Lance keeps it beneath their chapterhouse, in the heart of Aegis City. They parade the hoard through the streets as proof of their victory, and they keep the rest in a vault warded against lockpicks and magic alike.\"*\nThe dragon does not move from its seated position, the dark shadows of the cavern's rear hiding the stiffness in its wings. *\"Go. Take it all. And tell me what you will do for this prize.\"*"
    }
